From 0e0c4b8b0b4a453a4e360dbd1c786a2496b5196d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:59:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: base packets without enhancement units no
 longer restart the layer before it starts

While the enhancement layer waits, by picture order, for a picture to
start at and no place is being counted (rank.valid false), the base
pictures of the packets passed so far are of no further use: the layer
starts at a random-access picture of both layers, and every picture
before one in decoding order is presented before it (ITU-T H.265, 8.1).
The module let them go only for a packet with enhancement units (one
that the layer passes over, or one whose access unit of the layer cannot
be read). A run of packets without any, as in a stream whose layer starts
after base pictures of its own, filled the map of base pictures (64) and
the layer failed with "too many base pictures wait for their enhancement
pictures": Kodi started it again (ResyncDVEnhancement()), every 64
packets, and a random-access picture that came while the map was full
was lost for the start. Now the map is emptied at the end of such a
packet too, under the same condition.

Host test (the bench of the enhancement layer, its fel_rpu_test with a new option
lead=N that takes the enhancement units out of packets 1 to N, a single
track profile 7 FEL stream of 2877 pictures, as Kodi pairs them):
- before: lead=70, 200 and 500 started the layer again 1, 3 and 7 times
  for that reason, and the new check of the lead fails;
- after: none, the check passes; the pictures paired are the same ones
  and, picture for picture, the enhancement picture and the metadata of
  the whole run;
- the whole run, and the runs with a seek, starts in the middle, start
  codes, RPUs missing from the layer, an RPU that cannot be read, another
  display, the RPU in the base access unit, a hole, a strip and a base
  layer read as not reordered, give the same pictures, byte for byte,
  before and after; each passes or fails its checks alike before and
  after (the one with an unreadable RPU fails one check in both: its
  reference file was made for another copy of the stream).

The idea of letting go of the base pictures of such packets is
CroqueMr's (his build, #245 for #208); the condition and the place are
this module's own.
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
index 8c5b7da..92568ec 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
@@ -1517,6 +1517,16 @@ bool dvbridge_fel_submit(struct dvbridge_fel *f, const AVPacket *packet)
                     else
                         rank_try(f);
                 }
+                /* Hades: while the layer waits by picture order for a picture to start at and no place is being
+                 * counted, the base pictures of the packets passed so far are of no further use: the layer starts
+                 * at a random-access picture of both layers, and every picture before one in decoding order is
+                 * presented before it (ITU-T H.265, 8.1). They were let go only for a packet with enhancement
+                 * units (one that the layer passes over, or one that cannot be read, below); a run of packets
+                 * without any, as in a stream whose layer starts after base pictures of its own (CB1 #208),
+                 * filled the map and started the layer again ("too many base pictures wait") every 64 packets,
+                 * and a random-access picture that came while it was full was lost for the start. */
+                if (f->synchronizing && !f->timed && !f->rank.valid)
+                    f->num_times = 0;
                 return pump(f);
             }
             goto fail;
